# Parameter study: the (3.4.n.4) and (4.n.2n) vertices together, one row per n (Marek, 2 November 2026).
# n = 6 is the Euclidean plane, where the 2-uniform [3.4.6.4; 4.6.12] is one; from n = 7 on, the hyperbolic
# plane, where the two vertices close at one edge length too (checked for n = 7 to 10), so faces stay regular.

name hybrid_34n4_4n2n
k 1 3
vary n 6..10

angle A3
angle A4
angle A{n}
angle A{2n}

face A3 x 3
face A4 x 4
face A{n} x {n}
face A{2n} x {2n}

vertex A3 A4 A{n} A4
vertex A4 A{n} A{2n}

permutations no
